1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,560
The reason I'm such a fan of Rockefeller

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,040
is because of one very important lesson

3
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,600
that I learned from the letters that he sent his son,

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,000
which was he tells a story of how

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,080
he was the second largest oil producer,

6
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:12,800
and he went to go try and buy the largest producer.

7
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,280
And the guy rebuffed him a bunch of times

8
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,160
every time he tried to buy,

9
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:18,360
and then finally he was able to get a deal done,

10
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:23,040
and he way overpaid for this facility.

11
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,800
And the guy was laughing at him saying,

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,760
well, you know, you're an idiot,

13
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,800
I can't believe you paid this much for my business.

14
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:32,000
And then the next 30 days he did something like 24 deals.

15
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,920
And the reason he was able to do those 24 deals

16
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,440
is because once he was number two and bought the number one,

17
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,120
he had such a significant part of the market share

18
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,160
that he was able to say he was number one in the market.

19
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:44,560
And with that story, he was able to do 24 more deals

20
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,160
that were significantly more lucrative.

21
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:50,240
And so what I learned from that was the value of the story.

22
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,640
So there was the price of the assets in the business,

23
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,400
and then everything that he paid in excess,

24
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,580
he paid to do one thing,

25
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,900
which was to be able to say that he was number one,

26
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,660
so that he had the leverage in the rest of the negotiations.

27
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:03,140
And so it was really shifting from this, like,

28
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:05,180
I have to get an amazing deal in every single thing I do,

29
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:07,260
which happens across business all the time,

30
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:09,700
to taking a step back at the global outlook

31
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,540
of like battles and wars,

32
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:13,740
like I'm willing to lose battles to win wars.

